# Documents (keep windows adaptation docs)
#
# `docs/*` rather than `docs/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so the negations below were dead weight under
# `docs/` — the three tracked windows docs only escaped it because they were
# already in the index. `docs/*` still ignores everything under docs/, but lets
# an explicit negation actually take effect.
docs/*
!docs/windows-adaptation-standard.md
!docs/windows-p0-impl.md
!docs/windows-ui-blueprint.md
# Security audit ledger: open findings/observations for the SSH host-key trust
# audit. Tracked so an unfixed defect is recorded in the repository rather than
# only in a conversation, which is how it gets lost.
!docs/security-audit.md
# AI agent capability gap: the measured distance between Bonk's agent and the
# two reference implementations, plus the per-batch task records. Tracked for
# the same reason as the audit ledger — the open findings are the backlog, and
# a backlog that only exists in a conversation is a backlog that gets lost.
!docs/agent-capability-gap.md
!docs/agent-task-001-message-history.md
!docs/agent-task-002-anthropic-tool-use.md
!docs/agent-task-003-single-provider-resolution.md
!docs/agent-task-006-permission-parity.md
!docs/agent-task-007-remote-project-instructions.md
!docs/agent-task-008-agent-streaming.md
!docs/agent-task-009-agent-task-list.md
!docs/agent-task-010-host-scoped-allowlist.md
!docs/agent-task-004-agent-context-trust-boundary.md
!docs/agent-task-005-output-token-budget.md
!docs/agent-task-011-skills.md
!docs/agent-task-012-parallel-tools.md
!docs/agent-task-013-session-persistence.md
!docs/agent-task-014-mcp-client.md
!docs/agent-task-015-unicode-sanitization.md

